1. LICENSE GRANTED
On payment in full you get a perpetual, non-exclusive, non-transferable license
to install and use WARDEN for personal or commercial purposes on the number of
Macs your purchase covers:

  One Mac     1 machine
  Two Macs    2 machines
  Three Macs  3 machines

A machine may be replaced (a new Mac, a rebuilt Mac) without buying again. The
count limits how many machines run WARDEN at once, not how many you ever own.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
You may not redistribute, resell, sublicense, rent, or publish WARDEN or its
source. You may not share your license key beyond the seat count above, publish
it, or use it to generate keys. You may not remove or circumvent the license
check, and you may not distribute a build with it removed.

You may read, modify, and build the source for your own use on your licensed
machines. Modifying it does not extend the seat count and does not create a right
to distribute the result.

3. WHAT WARDEN DOES, STATED PLAINLY
WARDEN reads the on-disk transcripts your coding agents already write, indexes
them locally, and draws them. It does not write to your projects' source files.
It opens no network connection unless you explicitly turn on remote observation,
and that feature sends a redacted projection, never your prompts, paths, or file
contents. There is no telemetry and no account. License checking happens entirely
on your machine and contacts nothing.

